                    │     │   ├─→ Micro-steps (gradient accumulation)
                    │     │   │   ├─→ model(x, y) → cross-entropy loss
                    │     │   │   └─→ loss.backward() (accumulate grads)
                    │     │   │
                    │     │   ├─→ Schedule LR based on progress (warmup/warmdown)
                    │     │   ├─→ Update optimizer learning rates
                    │     │   ├─→ optimizer.step() [Muon + AdamW dispatch]
                    │     │   ├─→ model.zero_grad()
                    │     │   │
                    │     │   ├─→ Log: step, loss, lrm, dt, tok/sec, mfu%, epoch
                    │     │   │
                    │     │   └─→ Break if step > 10 AND total_training_time >= 300s
                    │     │
                    │     └─→ (If loss NaN or > 100: FAIL and exit(1))
                    │
                    ├─→ Final evaluation (val_bpb):
                    │     ├─→ Load val dataloader (shard_06542 only)
                    │     ├─→ For each eval batch:
                    │     │   ├─→ Forward pass
                    │     │   ├─→ Compute per-token cross-entropy (nats)
                    │     │   └─→ Lookup byte lengths from token_bytes.pt
                    │     ├─→ Sum nats & bytes across eval set (40M tokens)
                    │     └─→ BPB = total_nats / (ln(2) * total_bytes)
                    │
                    └─→ Print summary:
                          val_bpb: 0.997900
                          training_seconds: 300.1
                          peak_vram_mb: 45060.2
                          mfu_percent: 39.80
                          ... (8 more fields)
                              │
                              └─→ Output to stdout + captured in run.log
                                    │
Agent (outside repo) reads stdout
  │
  ├─→ grep "^val_bpb:\|^peak_vram_mb:" run.log
  │     └─→ Extract: val_bpb=0.9979, peak_vram=45060.2
  │
  ├─→ Compare to baseline (first run)
  │
  ├─→ Log to results.tsv:
  │     commit | val_bpb | memory_gb | status | description
  │     a1b2c3d | 0.9979 | 45.0 | [keep/discard/crash] | [reason]
  │
  └─→ Decision:
      ├─ If val_bpb < baseline: git stays (branch advances)
      └─ If val_bpb ≥ baseline: git reset --hard HEAD~1 (revert)
           │
           └─→ Loop back to editing train.py again
```

**Time Budget Enforcement:**

[train.py](train.py#L602-L604):
```python
if step > 10 and total_training_time >= TIME_BUDGET:
    break
```

Clock starts after 10 warmup steps to exclude compilation overhead.

