### **20. Weaknesses / Gaps**

#### **Architectural Gaps**

| Gap | Impact | Reason |
|-----|--------|--------|
| **No multi-agent orchestration** | Single agent can't explore design space in parallel | Minimalism; single GPU constraint |
| **No learned agent policy** | Agent uses cold LLM context every step (no RL-based improvement) | Tool-agnostic design; Karpathy intends "human-written program.md" optimization |
| **No curriculum learning** | Experiment sequence is random, not adaptive | Agent has no feedback loop beyond val_bpb |
| **No hyperparameter sensitivity analysis** | Difficult to understand which changes matter | No variance reduction; single val set |
| **No checkpointing** | Training aborted at 300s; can't resume mid-experiment | Intentional: fixed time budget = reproducible platform-agnostic results |
| **No meta-learning across runs** | Each run starts from scratch (no transfer) | Tokenizer is fixed; model weights reset; only code changes persist via git |

#### **Implementation Weaknesses**

| Weakness | Issue | Source |
|----------|-------|--------|
| **Gradient accumulation bug risk** | Agent could break `grad_accum_steps` calculation by changing `TOTAL_BATCH_SIZE` or `MAX_SEQ_LEN` without proportional model changes | [train.py](train.py#L463-L465): `assert TOTAL_BATCH_SIZE % tokens_per_fwdbwd == 0` can fail silently if agent edits wrong constant |
| **No git history cleanup** | After 100 experiments, branch has 100 commits; difficult to cherry-pick useful changes | git reset doesn't clean dangling commits; no squash/rebase automation |
| **VRAM is "soft" constraint** | Agent can easily OOM by increasing model depth; crash = "discard" but OOM might persist across attempts | [prepare.py](prepare.py#L356): Only evaluates on 40M tokens; may miss VRAM overages on larger val sets |
| **No LR schedule cross-validation** | Warmup/warmdown ratios are global; no per-layer scheduling | [train.py](train.py#L537-L551): Fixed schedules; agent must brute-force |
| **Flash Attention 3 GPU hard constraint** | Only works on Hopper+ (H100). Non-Hopper GPUs need kernels-community fallback | [train.py](train.py#L17-L19): Repo defaults to varunneal/flash-attention-3 but requires runtime detection |
| **Tokenizer is fixed** | Agent can't experiment with vocab size or tokenization strategy | [prepare.py](prepare.py#L38): VOCAB_SIZE=8192 hardcoded; BPE pattern fixed |

#### **Operational Gaps**

| Gap | Issue |
|-----|-------|
| **No crash recovery** | If OOM kills training mid-epoch, next run starts over without resuming | Intentional for simplicity |
| **No divergence detection** | Loss spikes > 100 hard-abort; no soft fail to reduce LR and retry | Fast fail is crude but prevents hanging |
| **No experiment deduplication** | Agent might accidentally test same hyperparams twice | Only human can spot in results.tsv |
| **TSV merge conflicts** | If two agents run in parallel, results.tsv merges can be messy | No distributed coordination |

#### **Design Constraints (Intentional)**

These aren't weaknesses but deliberate choices:

1. **Single File to Edit** — Keeps agent scope small; prevents systemic breakage
2. **No External Dependencies** — Reproducibility; no transitive deps to break
3. **No Distributed Training** — Keeps code simple; single GPU works on any HW
4. **Fixed Time Budget** — Platform-agnostic comparisons
5. **No Config Files** — Forces agent to engage with code structure

